</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:arca.fiocruz.br:icict/40900</identifier><datestamp>2026-10-17T18:30:22Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_icict_1956</setSpec><setSpec>col_icict_1957</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Toll-Like Receptor-2-Mediated C-C Chemokine Receptor 3 and Eotaxin-Driven Eosinophil Influx Induced by Mycobacterium bovis BCG Pleurisy</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>D&amp;apos;Avila, Heloisa</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Almeida, Patrícia E.</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Roque, Natália R.</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Faria Neto, Hugo Caire C.</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Bozza, Patrícia T.</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Influxo de Eosinófilos</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Eotaxina</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Mycobacterium bovis BCG Pleurisia</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Receptor C-C Mediado por Quimiocina</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Acesso aberto em 20/04/2020 - https://iai.asm.org/content/iai/75/3/1507.full.pdf</dc:description>
   <dc:description>An acute and persistent eosinophil infiltration is observed during Mycobacterium bovis BCG pleural infection in mice. Eosinophil accumulation, lipid body formation, and eotaxin production were significantly reduced in BCG-infected Toll-like receptor-2 (TLR2)-deficient mice compared to wild-type mice. Neutralization of eotaxin or CCR3 drastically inhibited BCG-induced eosinophil accumulation and lipid body formation, indicating that BCG-induced eosinophil recruitment and activation is largely dependent of TLR2-mediated eotaxin generation.</dc:description>
   <dc:description>2020-01-01</dc:description>
