</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:arca.fiocruz.br:icict/34777</identifier><datestamp>2026-10-25T14:10:13Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_icict_1744</setSpec><setSpec>col_icict_57384</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Ru(II)-thymine complex causes DNA damage and apoptotic cell death in human colon carcinoma HCT116 cells mediated by JNK/p38/ERK1/2 via a p53-independent signaling</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Silva, Suellen Leila Rocha</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Baliza, Ingrid Rayssa Souza</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Dias, Rosane Borges</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Sales, Caroline Brandi Schlaepfer</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Rocha, Clarissa Araújo Gurgel</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Soares, Milena Botelho Pereira</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Correa, Rodrigo de Souza</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Batista, Alzir Azevedo</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Bezerra, Daniel Pereira</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Carcinoma</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Câncer Colorretal</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Apoptose</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Células</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Morte Celular</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Rutênio</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>DOENÇAS [C]::Neoplasias::Neoplasias por Tipo Histológico::Neoplasias Epiteliais e Glandulares::Carcinoma</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>DOENÇAS [C]::Neoplasias::Neoplasias por Localização::Neoplasias do Sistema Digestório::Neoplasias Gastrointestinais::Neoplasias Intestinais::Neoplasias Colorretais</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>FENÔMENOS E PROCESSOS [G]::Fenômenos Fisiológicos Celulares::Morte Celular::Morte Celular Regulada::Apoptose</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>ANATOMIA [A]::Células</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>FENÔMENOS E PROCESSOS [G]::Fenômenos Fisiológicos Celulares::Morte Celular</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>COMPOSTOS QUÍMICOS E DROGAS [D]::Compostos Inorgânicos::Elementos Químicos::Metais Pesados::Rutênio</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Coordenação de Aperfeiçoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior (CAPES), Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Científico e Tecnológico (CNPq), Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado da Bahia (FAPESB) and Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo (FAPESP). R.S. Correa would like to thank the financial support provided by the CNPq (Grant 403588/2016-2 and 308370/2017-1) and FAPEMIG (APQ-01674-18).</dc:description>
   <dc:description>Ru(II)-thymine complex [Ru(PPh3)2(Thy)(bipy)]PF6 (where PPh3 = triphenylphosphine, Thy = thyminate and bipy = 2,2&amp;apos;-bipyridine) is a potent cytotoxic agent with ability to bind to DNA, inducing caspase-mediated apoptosis in leukemia cells. In this study, we investigated the mechanism underlying the cell death induction by Ru(II)-thymine complex in human colon carcinoma HCT116 cells, as well as its effect in xenograft tumor model. The Ru(II)-thymine complex increased significantly the percentage of apoptotic HCT116 cells. Co-treatment with a JNK/SAPK inhibitor, p38 MAPK inhibitor and MEK inhibitor, which inhibit the activation of ERK1/2, caused a marked reduction of the percentage of complex-induced apoptotic cells. Moreover, the Ru(II)-thymine complex induced an increase in phospho-JNK2 (T183/Y185), phospho-p38α (T180/Y182) and phospho-ERK1 (T202/Y204) levels in HCT116 cells. Treatment with the Ru(II)-thymine complex increased significantly the phospho-histone H2AX (S139) expression, a DNA damage marker. The expression of phospho-p53 (S15) and MDM2 were not changed, and the co-treatment with a p53 inhibitor (cyclic pifithrin-α) did not reduce the complex-induced apoptosis in HCT116 cells, indicating that the Ru(II)-thymine complex induces DNA damage-mediated apoptosis by JNK/p38/ERK1/2 via a p53-independent signaling. The Ru(II)-thymine complex (1 and 2 mg/kg/day) also inhibited HCT116 cell growth in a xenograft model, reducing the tumor mass at 32.6-40.1%. Altogether, indicate that the Ru(II)-thymine complex is a promising anti-colon cancer drug candidate.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2019-08-13T17:08:42Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2019-08-13T17:08:42Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2019</dc:date>
   <dc:type>journal article</dc:type>
   <dc:identifier>SILVA, Suellen Leila Rocha et al. Ru(II)-thymine complex causes DNA damage and apoptotic cell death in human colon carcinoma HCT116 cells mediated by JNK/p38/ERK1/2 via a p53-independent signaling. Scientific Reports, v. 9, p. 1-11, 2019.</dc:identifier>
