   <dc:title>Cestóides Proteocefalídeos de &amp;quot;Cachara&amp;quot;, Pseudoplatystoma Fasciatus (L.) (Pisces, Pimelodidae) de Mato Grosso</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Rego, Amilcar Arandas</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Cachara</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Pseudoplatystoma Fasciatus</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Parasitos de Peixes</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Cestódeos</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Mato Grosso</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Proteocefálida</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>ORGANISMOS [B]::Eucariotos::Animais::Invertebrados::Helmintos::Platelmintos::Cestoides</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>14 Vida na água</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>The author describes three species of protcocephalid cestodes from the Pimelodid fish, Pseudoplatystoma fasciatus (L.) from rivers of Mato Grosso, Brazil: Nomimoscolex lopesi sp. n., Peltidocotyle rugosa Diesing, 1850 and Spatulifer rugosa (Woodland, 1935). P. rugosa is for the first time referred in this fish species. One hyperparasite nematode specimen was found in a strobila of S. rugosa.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2020-09-11T18:15:16Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2020-09-11T18:15:16Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>1989</dc:date>
   <dc:type>journal article</dc:type>
